["<aside class=\"callout why\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Why it matters</div><p>Most mule deer are seen in two short windows a day. Be in the right seat for both.</p></aside><figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 340\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"A 24 hour clock with midnight at the top. Orange activity peaks about 04:00 to 09:00 and 17:00 to 21:00. Green: bedded about 10:00 to 15:00. Night: feeding on and off.\">\n<rect width=\"400\" height=\"340\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"17\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">A late October day</text><circle cx=\"200\" cy=\"160\" r=\"110\" fill=\"#d9dfe8\"/><path d=\"M295.3 105.0 A 110 110 0 0 1 277.8 237.8 L242.4 202.4 A 60 60 0 0 0 252.0 130.0 Z\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><path d=\"M93.7 188.5 A 110 110 0 0 1 122.2 82.2 L157.6 117.6 A 60 60 0 0 0 142.0 175.5 Z\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><path d=\"M255.0 255.3 A 110 110 0 0 1 122.2 237.8 L157.6 202.4 A 60 60 0 0 0 230.0 212.0 Z\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/><path d=\"M122.2 82.2 A 110 110 0 0 1 200.0 50.0 L200.0 100.0 A 60 60 0 0 0 157.6 117.6 Z\" fill=\"#b9c3d6\"/><path d=\"M200.0 50.0 A 110 110 0 0 1 295.3 105.0 L252.0 130.0 A 60 60 0 0 0 200.0 100.0 Z\" fill=\"#b9c3d6\"/><circle cx=\"200\" cy=\"160\" r=\"58\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"41\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">00</text><text x=\"288\" y=\"77\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">03</text><text x=\"324\" y=\"165\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">06</text><text x=\"288\" y=\"253\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">09</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"289\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">12</text><text x=\"112\" y=\"253\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">15</text><text x=\"76\" y=\"165\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">18</text><text x=\"112\" y=\"77\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">21</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"154\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">24 hours</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"174\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#6b4f35\" text-anchor=\"middle\">midnight top</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"290\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"30\" y=\"302\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">peaks 04 to 09, 17 to 21</text><rect x=\"230\" y=\"290\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/><text x=\"250\" y=\"302\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">bedded 10 to 15</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"326\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#6b4f35\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Night: on and off feeding (75 to 85%)</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Peaks about 04:00 to 09:00 and 17:00 to 21:00 <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li><li>Bedded about 10:00 to 15:00 <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: what this chapter covers</summary><ul><li>Bed to feed to water, the hours, and how wind, rain, snow, cold fronts, barometric pressure, the moon and hunting pressure change the day.</li><li>Each claim carries its evidence level. Much of what hunters say about weather is lore, not tested (see the evidence screen).</li><li>Previous: <a href=\"#/s/mc-mule-deer-05\">Chapter 5, The year</a>. Next: <a href=\"#/s/mc-mule-deer-07\">Chapter 7, Where they are</a>.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Side view of one slope. Water at the bottom, an open feeding slope in the middle, and a bed on a bench below timber near the top with a view down. In the morning deer drift up to bed; in the evening they come down to feed and water. A pattern, not a law.\">\n<rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"17\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Bed, feed, water: one slope</text><path d=\"M0 280 L80 260 L170 200 L230 150 L250 140 L300 132 L340 90 L400 60 L400 300 L0 300 Z\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><path d=\"M0 290 Q 60 284 120 290 L120 300 L0 300 Z\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\"/><text x=\"20\" y=\"284\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">water</text><polygon points=\"300,128 308,102 316,128\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><polygon points=\"318,112 326,86 334,112\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><polygon points=\"282,132 290,106 298,132\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><ellipse cx=\"262\" cy=\"136\" rx=\"16\" ry=\"6\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><text x=\"190\" y=\"96\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">bed: bench below cover,</text><text x=\"190\" y=\"114\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">view down the slope</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"228\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">feed: open slope</text><path d=\"M120 250 Q 180 200 250 142\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-dasharray=\"6 5\"/><line x1=\"200\" y1=\"186\" x2=\"214\" y2=\"174\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><polygon points=\"214.0,174.0 210.0,183.2 204.3,176.6\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"176\" y=\"168\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-weight=\"bold\">morning: up</text><path d=\"M240 160 Q 170 230 100 268\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-dasharray=\"6 5\"/><line x1=\"130\" y1=\"252\" x2=\"116\" y2=\"260\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><polygon points=\"116.0,260.0 121.7,251.8 126.0,259.3\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\"/><text x=\"214\" y=\"236\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">evening: down</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"60\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#6b4f35\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Pattern, not a law (Tip)</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Dawn: feed on open slopes, then drift up to bed <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li></ul><ul><li>Dusk: down to feed, water in dry weather (80%, Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the daily loop</summary><aside class=\"callout warn\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Warning</div><p>Study aid only. The official regulations are the law.</p></aside><ul><li>Night: feeds on and off in open grass and brush, rests between bouts <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>Before first light to about 09:00: a strong activity peak (85%, Stewart and others 2002, Oregon telemetry).</li><li>Then it drifts uphill or into cover to bed (85%, quick lesson).</li><li>Mule deer \"tend to bed not far from a food source\" (65%, Rinella).</li><li>Midday: bedded, chewing cud; gets up to stretch, nibble and re bed <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>Late afternoon: rises, browses near the bed, then moves to open feeding slopes <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>Sunset to about 21:00: second peak <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li><li>Water: in dry fall weather near water at dusk or dawn; with green feed and dew, less need (Tip).</li><li>Deer activity is highest within about 3 hours of sunrise and sunset (85%, Mule Deer Working Group fact sheet 17).</li><li>Legal hunting hours: 1 hour before sunrise to 1 hour after sunset (99%, page 11, see <a href=\"#/s/rb-legal-methods\">legal methods</a>).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram anim\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Animation of a mule deer day in late October, side view of a slope. Midday, about 10:00 to 15:00, the deer is bedded in timber near the top, chewing cud. From about 16:00 it rises, browses and walks down to the open feeding slope, feeding until about 21:00. In a dry fall it drinks near water at dusk or dawn, a tip. It feeds on and off through the night. The big morning feed runs about 04:00 to 09:00. After sunrise it drifts uphill back to the timber and beds. Lesson: be glassing before legal light.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<path d=\"M0 300 L0 70 Q120 80 200 150 Q290 220 400 240 L400 300 Z\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><polygon points=\"9.0,80 20,47.0 31.0,80\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><rect x=\"17.8\" y=\"80\" width=\"4.4\" height=\"6.6000000000000005\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><polygon points=\"34.0,78 45,45.0 56.0,78\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><rect x=\"42.8\" y=\"78\" width=\"4.4\" height=\"6.6000000000000005\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><polygon points=\"59.0,84 70,51.0 81.0,84\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><rect x=\"67.8\" y=\"84\" width=\"4.4\" height=\"6.6000000000000005\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><polygon points=\"84.0,90 95,57.0 106.0,90\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><rect x=\"92.8\" y=\"90\" width=\"4.4\" height=\"6.6000000000000005\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><polygon points=\"109.0,98 120,65.0 131.0,98\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><rect x=\"117.8\" y=\"98\" width=\"4.4\" height=\"6.6000000000000005\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><polygon points=\"24.0,104 35,71.0 46.0,104\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><rect x=\"32.8\" y=\"104\" width=\"4.4\" height=\"6.6000000000000005\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><polygon points=\"49.0,108 60,75.0 71.0,108\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><rect x=\"57.8\" y=\"108\" width=\"4.4\" height=\"6.6000000000000005\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><text x=\"10\" y=\"140\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\">Bed: timber</text><text x=\"190\" y=\"214\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\">Feed: open slope</text><path d=\"M250 285 Q330 262 400 270 L400 300 L240 300 Z\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" opacity=\".7\"/><text x=\"300\" y=\"294\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"start\">Water</text><path id=\"sa-deer-day-path\" d=\"M80 112 L220 180 L320 262 L220 180 L80 112\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-dasharray=\"5 6\" opacity=\".6\"/><g><g transform=\"translate(0 -12)\"><g><g transform=\"translate(0 0) scale(0.32 0.32)\"><rect x=\"-30\" y=\"6\" width=\"7\" height=\"38\" rx=\"3.5\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><rect x=\"-21\" y=\"6\" width=\"7\" height=\"38\" rx=\"3.5\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><rect x=\"22\" y=\"6\" width=\"7\" height=\"38\" rx=\"3.5\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><rect x=\"31\" y=\"6\" width=\"7\" height=\"38\" rx=\"3.5\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><ellipse cx=\"0\" cy=\"0\" rx=\"42\" ry=\"17\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><ellipse cx=\"-37\" cy=\"-2\" rx=\"8\" ry=\"11\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><path d=\"M-42 -6 Q-47 4 -45 14\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"4\" fill=\"none\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><path d=\"M-45 10 L-45 16\" stroke=\"#111\" stroke-width=\"5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><path d=\"M26 -10 L42 -40 L56 -36 L40 6 Z\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><ellipse cx=\"56\" cy=\"-40\" rx=\"14\" ry=\"7\" transform=\"rotate(18 56 -40)\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><ellipse cx=\"42\" cy=\"-50\" rx=\"11\" ry=\"4.5\" transform=\"rotate(-35 42 -50)\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"58\" cy=\"-42\" r=\"1.8\" fill=\"#23261f\"/><path d=\"M48 -46 L50 -62 M50 -62 L42 -76 M50 -62 L60 -72 M42 -76 L36 -88 M42 -76 L48 -90 M60 -72 L58 -86 M60 -72 L70 -82\" stroke=\"#6b4f35\" stroke-width=\"3.5\" fill=\"none\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/></g><set attributeName=\"transform\" to=\"scale(-1 1)\" begin=\"5.6s\"/></g></g><animateMotion dur=\"10s\" fill=\"freeze\" calcMode=\"linear\" keyPoints=\"0;0;0.27;0.5;0.5;0.5;0.73;0.73;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.15;0.33;0.45;0.5;0.56;0.64;0.8;0.95;1\"><mpath href=\"#sa-deer-day-path\"/></animateMotion></g><g opacity=\"1\"><set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"1\" begin=\"0s\"/><set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"0\" begin=\"1.5s\"/><rect x=\"150\" y=\"8\" width=\"244\" height=\"54\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><text x=\"162\" y=\"30\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"start\">10:00 to 15:00</text><text x=\"162\" y=\"52\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"start\">Bedded, chewing cud</text></g><g opacity=\"0\"><set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"1\" begin=\"1.5s\"/><set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"0\" begin=\"4.2s\"/><rect x=\"150\" y=\"8\" width=\"244\" height=\"54\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><text x=\"162\" y=\"30\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"start\">16:00 to 21:00</text><text x=\"162\" y=\"52\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"start\">Rises, browses, walks out to feed</text></g><g opacity=\"0\"><set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"1\" begin=\"4.2s\"/><set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"0\" begin=\"5.6s\"/><rect x=\"150\" y=\"8\" width=\"244\" height=\"54\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><text x=\"162\" y=\"30\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"start\">Dusk or dawn, dry fall</text><text x=\"162\" y=\"52\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"start\">Drinks near water (Tip)</text></g><g opacity=\"0\"><set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"1\" begin=\"5.6s\"/><set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"0\" begin=\"6.4s\"/><rect x=\"150\" y=\"8\" width=\"244\" height=\"54\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><text x=\"162\" y=\"30\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"start\">Night</text><text x=\"162\" y=\"52\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"start\">Feeds on and off, rests</text></g><g opacity=\"0\"><set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"1\" begin=\"6.4s\"/><set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"0\" begin=\"8.0s\"/><rect x=\"150\" y=\"8\" width=\"244\" height=\"54\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><text x=\"162\" y=\"30\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"start\">04:00 to 09:00</text><text x=\"162\" y=\"52\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"start\">Big morning feed</text></g><g opacity=\"0\"><set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"1\" begin=\"8.0s\"/><set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"0\" begin=\"9.6s\"/><rect x=\"150\" y=\"8\" width=\"244\" height=\"54\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><text x=\"162\" y=\"30\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"start\">After sunrise</text><text x=\"162\" y=\"52\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"start\">Drifts uphill to cover</text></g><g opacity=\"0\"><set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"1\" begin=\"9.6s\"/><rect x=\"150\" y=\"8\" width=\"244\" height=\"54\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"162\" y=\"30\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"start\">Your move</text><text x=\"162\" y=\"52\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"start\">Be glassing before legal light</text></g>\n</svg>\n<figcaption>Bed, feed, water, feed, bed. <button class=\"anim-replay\">↻ Replay</button></figcaption></figure>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Where a deer beds today. Warm day: in north facing timber, benches, draws and shade. Cold day: on a sunny south or west slope, out of the wind, here tucked below a rock.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Where a deer beds today</text><rect x=\"8\" y=\"40\" width=\"188\" height=\"252\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"/><text x=\"20\" y=\"64\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" text-anchor=\"start\">Warm day</text><polygon points=\"35.0,190 48,151.0 61.0,190\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><rect x=\"45.4\" y=\"190\" width=\"5.2\" height=\"7.800000000000001\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><polygon points=\"59.0,182 72,143.0 85.0,182\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><rect x=\"69.4\" y=\"182\" width=\"5.2\" height=\"7.800000000000001\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><polygon points=\"83.0,174 96,135.0 109.0,174\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><rect x=\"93.4\" y=\"174\" width=\"5.2\" height=\"7.800000000000001\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><polygon points=\"107.0,166 120,127.0 133.0,166\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><rect x=\"117.4\" y=\"166\" width=\"5.2\" height=\"7.800000000000001\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><polygon points=\"131.0,158 144,119.0 157.0,158\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><rect x=\"141.4\" y=\"158\" width=\"5.2\" height=\"7.800000000000001\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><ellipse cx=\"104\" cy=\"196\" rx=\"18\" ry=\"7\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><circle cx=\"168\" cy=\"96\" r=\"12\" fill=\"#f2c94c\" opacity=\".5\"/><text x=\"20\" y=\"244\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">North facing timber,</text><text x=\"20\" y=\"264\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">benches, draws, shade</text><rect x=\"204\" y=\"40\" width=\"188\" height=\"252\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"/><text x=\"216\" y=\"64\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"start\">Cold day</text><path d=\"M214 210 Q294 150 382 120 L382 210 Z\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/><circle cx=\"244\" cy=\"96\" r=\"16\" fill=\"#f2c94c\"/><line x1=\"264\" y1=\"100\" x2=\"304\" y2=\"120\" stroke=\"#f2c94c\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><line x1=\"264\" y1=\"110\" x2=\"304\" y2=\"134\" stroke=\"#f2c94c\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><line x1=\"264\" y1=\"120\" x2=\"304\" y2=\"148\" stroke=\"#f2c94c\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><ellipse cx=\"324\" cy=\"162\" rx=\"18\" ry=\"7\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><rect x=\"344\" y=\"150\" width=\"30\" height=\"12\" fill=\"#9c8a76\"/><text x=\"344\" y=\"144\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\">rock</text><text x=\"216\" y=\"244\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Sunny south or west</text><text x=\"216\" y=\"264\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">slope, out of the wind</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Warm day: shade, north slopes, timber <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li></ul><ul><li>Cold day: sun, south and west slopes, out of wind <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: where it beds and why</summary><ul><li>Day beds give hiding cover and shelter (80%, Germaine 2004).</li><li>Warm days: north facing timber, benches, draws, shade <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>Cold days: sunny south and west slopes out of the wind <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>On a slope it often beds facing downhill with the wind at its back, on the leeward side of a roll (65%, Rinella).</li><li>In a desert study, bed sites had the most overhead cover in summer (60%, Arizona 2001). Temperature and canopy decide summer beds <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">60%</span>.</li><li>Lore: bucks bed in the top third of a slope (60%, not a rule).</li><li>Midday is the time to find beds with binoculars and plan a stalk (Tip, chapter 9).</li></ul></details>","<div class=\"gallery\"><figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/g-md-does-bedded.jpg\" alt=\"Bedded does: heads and ears above the brush.\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Bedded does: heads and ears above the brush. <span class=\"credit\">Photo: USFWS Mountain-Prairie, Public domain, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mule_Deer_Bedded_Down_in_Sagebrush_and_Snow_(15523121163).jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure><figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/g-md-buck-bedded.jpg\" alt=\"Bedded buck: only the rack gives it away.\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Bedded buck: only the rack gives it away. <span class=\"credit\">Photo: USFWS Mountain-Prairie, Public domain, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mule_Deer_Buck_in_Southwest_Wyoming_(23007137314).jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure></div>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Three boxes for a storm day, hunter lore only. Before: feeding hard. During: bedded tight. After: up and moving. Widely told, weakly tested. Strong or shifting wind ruins a steady wind for stalks. Go anyway and log what you see.\">\n<rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"17\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">A storm day, hunter lore (Tip)</text><rect x=\"14\" y=\"50\" width=\"118\" height=\"150\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/><text x=\"73\" y=\"80\" font-size=\"17\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Before</text><text x=\"73\" y=\"112\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Feeding hard?</text><rect x=\"142\" y=\"50\" width=\"118\" height=\"150\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#7d7468\"/><text x=\"201\" y=\"80\" font-size=\"17\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">During</text><text x=\"201\" y=\"112\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Bedded tight</text><line x1=\"162\" y1=\"140\" x2=\"154\" y2=\"170\" stroke=\"#fffaf0\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><line x1=\"182\" y1=\"140\" x2=\"174\" y2=\"170\" stroke=\"#fffaf0\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><line x1=\"202\" y1=\"140\" x2=\"194\" y2=\"170\" stroke=\"#fffaf0\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><line x1=\"222\" y1=\"140\" x2=\"214\" y2=\"170\" stroke=\"#fffaf0\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><line x1=\"242\" y1=\"140\" x2=\"234\" y2=\"170\" stroke=\"#fffaf0\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><rect x=\"270\" y=\"50\" width=\"118\" height=\"150\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"329\" y=\"80\" font-size=\"17\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">After</text><text x=\"329\" y=\"112\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Up and moving</text><line x1=\"132\" y1=\"125\" x2=\"142\" y2=\"125\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><polygon points=\"142.0,125.0 133.0,129.3 133.0,120.7\" fill=\"#23261f\"/><line x1=\"260\" y1=\"125\" x2=\"270\" y2=\"125\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><polygon points=\"270.0,125.0 261.0,129.3 261.0,120.7\" fill=\"#23261f\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"230\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Widely told, weakly tested (50 to 55%)</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"250\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Strong wind kills a steady wind for stalks (65%)</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"280\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Go anyway. Log what you see in the Journal.</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Strong or shifting wind ruins stalks <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li><li>Most weather effects on deer are weakly tested (50 to 55%).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: weather, one by one</summary><ul><li><strong>Wind:</strong> strong wind makes deer edgy and hard to approach (Tip, hunter lore 55%). Clouds and incoming weather kill a steady wind; back out and wait (65%, Rinella).</li><li><strong>Rain:</strong> light rain dampens your noise and scent; deer often feed through it (Tip). Heavy rain: bedded (Tip).</li><li><strong>Snow:</strong> fresh snow shows every track (Tip). Deep snow pushes deer down and limits movement (85%, chapter 5).</li><li><strong>Cold:</strong> cold, crisp mornings put rutting animals on their feet in daylight; warm wind hides them (70%, <a href=\"#/s/the-rut\">the rut</a>).</li><li><strong>Heat:</strong> warm October afternoons push deer into shade and timber <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li><strong>Cold fronts:</strong> hunters say deer feed hard before a front and move after it (Tip, 50%). Not well tested for mule deer.</li><li>In GPS (Global Positioning System) studies of white tails, weather had an inconsistent effect within a season (70%, Webb and others 2010).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Bars of how strong the evidence is that each thing changes deer movement. Strong: dawn and dusk light, snow and cold. Good: hunting pressure, the November rut. Weak: wind and rain, barometer. Moon phase: GPS studies found no effect.\">\n<rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"17\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">What moves deer? Evidence strength</text><text x=\"150\" y=\"64\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"end\">Dawn and dusk light</text><rect x=\"158\" y=\"50\" width=\"200\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#ece6da\"/><rect x=\"158\" y=\"50\" width=\"170\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"150\" y=\"98\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"end\">Snow and cold</text><rect x=\"158\" y=\"84\" width=\"200\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#ece6da\"/><rect x=\"158\" y=\"84\" width=\"170\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"150\" y=\"132\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"end\">Hunting pressure</text><rect x=\"158\" y=\"118\" width=\"200\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#ece6da\"/><rect x=\"158\" y=\"118\" width=\"140\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><text x=\"150\" y=\"166\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"end\">Rut (Nov)</text><rect x=\"158\" y=\"152\" width=\"200\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#ece6da\"/><rect x=\"158\" y=\"152\" width=\"150\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><text x=\"150\" y=\"200\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"end\">Wind, rain</text><rect x=\"158\" y=\"186\" width=\"200\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#ece6da\"/><rect x=\"158\" y=\"186\" width=\"100\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/><text x=\"150\" y=\"234\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"end\">Barometer</text><rect x=\"158\" y=\"220\" width=\"200\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#ece6da\"/><rect x=\"158\" y=\"220\" width=\"80\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/><text x=\"150\" y=\"268\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"end\">Moon phase</text><rect x=\"158\" y=\"254\" width=\"200\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#ece6da\"/><rect x=\"158\" y=\"254\" width=\"50\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#b9b0a0\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"292\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#6b4f35\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Moon: GPS studies found no effect (70%)</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Moon phase: GPS (Global Positioning System) collar studies found no effect <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>Barometer: no solid evidence (40%, Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the evidence, honestly</summary><ul><li>Moon: 32 GPS collared white tails in Oklahoma over 7 years. Moon phase had no effect on daily, night or day movement (70%, Webb and others 2010). Other GPS work found small or no moon effects <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li><li>Earlier studies that found moon effects used older radio collars (65%, Penn State).</li><li>No mule deer moon study found. Treat moon tables as entertainment (Tip).</li><li>Barometric pressure: one white tail study tied very high pressure to more winter buck movement, with caveats; others found little (50%, search previews). Not a fact for mule deer.</li><li>What does move deer, with good evidence: light (dawn and dusk), snow and cold, the rut, hunting pressure (70 to 85%).</li><li>My lean: hunt every day you can. Log weather and sightings in the Journal and find your own pattern (Tip).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram anim\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Animation, top view. Before the opener, deer feed in an open field near the road. On opening day trucks park along the road. The deer move away from the road into thick timber. One hunter walks past the last truck, deep into the thick cover where the deer went.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#efe6cf\"/>\n  <path d=\"M240 0 L400 0 L400 300 L270 300 C 250 220, 300 120, 240 0 Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" opacity=\".75\"/>\n  <text x=\"330\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">thick timber</text>\n  <rect x=\"0\" y=\"250\" width=\"400\" height=\"22\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\" opacity=\".6\"/>\n  <text x=\"12\" y=\"292\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">road</text>\n  <g fill=\"#8b5a2b\">\n    <g><ellipse rx=\"12\" ry=\"6\"/><animateTransform attributeName=\"transform\" type=\"translate\" values=\"80 180;80 180;300 120;300 120\" keyTimes=\"0;0.35;0.7;1\" dur=\"9s\" fill=\"freeze\" calcMode=\"linear\"/></g>\n    <g><ellipse rx=\"12\" ry=\"6\"/><animateTransform attributeName=\"transform\" type=\"translate\" values=\"130 200;130 200;330 170;330 170\" keyTimes=\"0;0.38;0.72;1\" dur=\"9s\" fill=\"freeze\"/></g>\n    <g><ellipse rx=\"12\" ry=\"6\"/><animateTransform attributeName=\"transform\" type=\"translate\" values=\"170 160;170 160;350 90;350 90\" keyTimes=\"0;0.4;0.75;1\" dur=\"9s\" fill=\"freeze\"/></g>\n  </g>\n  <g fill=\"#4a7fb0\" opacity=\"0\"><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"0;1\" begin=\"2.4s\" dur=\".4s\" fill=\"freeze\"/>\n    <rect x=\"40\" y=\"254\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" rx=\"3\"/><rect x=\"90\" y=\"254\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" rx=\"3\"/><rect x=\"140\" y=\"254\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" rx=\"3\"/><rect x=\"190\" y=\"254\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" rx=\"3\"/></g>\n  <g opacity=\"1\"><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"1;0\" begin=\"2.4s\" dur=\".3s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><text x=\"12\" y=\"40\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">Before opening day</text></g>\n  <g opacity=\"0\"><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"0;1\" begin=\"2.4s\" dur=\".3s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><text x=\"12\" y=\"40\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#c0392b\">Opener: trucks arrive</text></g>\n  <path id=\"hf-pressure-shift-path\" d=\"M260 261 C 262 230, 262 200, 280 160\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" stroke-dasharray=\"5 5\" opacity=\"0\"><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"0;1\" begin=\"6.5s\" dur=\".3s\" fill=\"freeze\"/></path>\n  <circle r=\"8\" fill=\"#e8590c\" opacity=\"0\"><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"0;1\" begin=\"6.5s\" dur=\".3s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><animateMotion begin=\"6.5s\" dur=\"2.2s\" fill=\"freeze\"><mpath href=\"#hf-pressure-shift-path\"/></animateMotion></circle>\n  <g opacity=\"0\"><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"0;1\" begin=\"8.5s\" dur=\".4s\" fill=\"freeze\"/>\n    <rect x=\"12\" y=\"60\" width=\"210\" height=\"50\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/>\n    <text x=\"117\" y=\"82\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Walk past the last truck</text>\n    <text x=\"117\" y=\"100\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Hunt the thick stuff (Tip)</text></g>\n</svg>\n<figcaption>Pressure pushes deer into thick cover. <button class=\"anim-replay\">↻ Replay</button></figcaption></figure><ul><li>Pressured deer use thicker cover and more night (65 to 70%).</li><li>Weekends and roads push deer away (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: pressure in detail</summary><aside class=\"callout warn\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Warning</div><p>Study aid only. The official regulations are the law.</p></aside><ul><li>Pressured deer move more at night and use thicker cover (70%, quick lesson).</li><li>Arizona: hunted deer shifted to better escape cover as the season went on <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>. Montana: more use of timber in hunting season <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li><li>Hunted populations flee people at longer distances (65%, Stankowich 2008).</li><li>Roads and ATVs (all terrain vehicles) raise buck vulnerability (65%, Idaho Fish and Game).</li><li>Off trail people and dogs disturb more than on trail (85%, fact sheet 17).</li><li>For you: be in your seat before first light, stay through midday on busy weekends, and hunt the quiet weekdays if you can (Tip).</li><li>Rule recap (study aid only): no ATV (all terrain vehicle) for hunting 1 September to 10 December in MUs (Management Units) 3-28, 3-29 and 3-30 (99%, page 33, <a href=\"#/s/rb-region-3\">Region 3</a>). Fewer quads, calmer deer (Tip).</li></ul></details>","<div class=\"tbl\"><table><thead><tr><th>Period</th><th>Day pattern (certainty)</th><th>Your move (Tip)</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>September</td><td>Dawn and dusk peaks, beds high <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span></td><td>Glass basins at first light</td></tr><tr><td>October</td><td>Same, bucks start roaming late month <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span></td><td>Sit glassing seats dawn and dusk</td></tr><tr><td>November rut</td><td>Bucks move all day near does (65 to 75%)</td><td>Glass doe groups all day</td></tr><tr><td>December</td><td>Post rut, bucks hide and rest <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">90%</span></td><td>Slow glassing of thick edges</td></tr></tbody></table></div><ul><li>Rut days are long days: stay out (65%, Rinella).</li><li>Post rut bucks hide <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">90%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: why</summary><ul><li>Peaks at dawn and dusk come from the Starkey study <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span> and agency advice (85%, fact sheet 17).</li><li>Rut: bucks travel and show in daylight (75%, <a href=\"#/s/the-rut\">the rut</a>); \"hunt all day\" (65%, Rinella).</li><li>Post rut: \"they tend to hide and rest\" (90%, BC account).</li></ul></details>","<div class=\"tbl\"><table><thead><tr><th>Claim</th><th>Evidence</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Dawn and dusk peaks</td><td>Strong <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span></td></tr><tr><td>Snow pushes deer down</td><td>Strong <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span></td></tr><tr><td>Pressure shifts deer to cover</td><td>Good (65 to 70%)</td></tr><tr><td>Rut brings bucks out by day</td><td>Good <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span></td></tr><tr><td>Feeding before a front</td><td>Lore <span class=\"cert c-tip\" title=\"Certainty\">50%</span></td></tr><tr><td>Barometer rules movement</td><td>Weak <span class=\"cert c-tip\" title=\"Certainty\">40%</span></td></tr><tr><td>Moon phase rules movement</td><td>Not supported (70% for no effect)</td></tr></tbody></table></div><ul><li>Plan on light, snow, rut and pressure. Log the rest (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: how to read this</summary><ul><li>Strong: several studies or agency sources agree.</li><li>Good: one or two studies, or agency advice.</li><li>Lore: widely told by hunters, not tested for mule deer.</li><li>Weak or not supported: tested, little or no effect found, mostly in white tails.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 340\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"A 24 hour clock with midnight at the top. Orange activity peaks about 04:00 to 09:00 and 17:00 to 21:00. Green: bedded about 10:00 to 15:00. Night: feeding on and off.\">\n<rect width=\"400\" height=\"340\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"17\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">A late October day</text><circle cx=\"200\" cy=\"160\" r=\"110\" fill=\"#d9dfe8\"/><path d=\"M295.3 105.0 A 110 110 0 0 1 277.8 237.8 L242.4 202.4 A 60 60 0 0 0 252.0 130.0 Z\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><path d=\"M93.7 188.5 A 110 110 0 0 1 122.2 82.2 L157.6 117.6 A 60 60 0 0 0 142.0 175.5 Z\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><path d=\"M255.0 255.3 A 110 110 0 0 1 122.2 237.8 L157.6 202.4 A 60 60 0 0 0 230.0 212.0 Z\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/><path d=\"M122.2 82.2 A 110 110 0 0 1 200.0 50.0 L200.0 100.0 A 60 60 0 0 0 157.6 117.6 Z\" fill=\"#b9c3d6\"/><path d=\"M200.0 50.0 A 110 110 0 0 1 295.3 105.0 L252.0 130.0 A 60 60 0 0 0 200.0 100.0 Z\" fill=\"#b9c3d6\"/><circle cx=\"200\" cy=\"160\" r=\"58\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"41\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">00</text><text x=\"288\" y=\"77\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">03</text><text x=\"324\" y=\"165\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">06</text><text x=\"288\" y=\"253\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">09</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"289\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">12</text><text x=\"112\" y=\"253\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">15</text><text x=\"76\" y=\"165\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">18</text><text x=\"112\" y=\"77\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">21</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"154\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">24 hours</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"174\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#6b4f35\" text-anchor=\"middle\">midnight top</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"290\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"30\" y=\"302\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">peaks 04 to 09, 17 to 21</text><rect x=\"230\" y=\"290\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/><text x=\"250\" y=\"302\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">bedded 10 to 15</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"326\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#6b4f35\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Night: on and off feeding (75 to 85%)</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li><strong>Rhyme:</strong> \"Four to nine and five to nine; between them deer lie down in line.\"</li><li><strong>Number trick:</strong> 3 hours: peak activity within 3 hours of sunrise and sunset <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li><li><strong>Old hand's rule</strong> (tradition): \"Be on the glass before the light.\"</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: more hooks</summary><ul><li><strong>Rhyme:</strong> \"Hot day, shady slope; cold day, sunny hope.\"</li><li><strong>Number trick:</strong> 04 to 09, 10 to 15, 17 to 21: active, bedded, active (80 to 85%).</li><li><strong>Number trick:</strong> 32 deer, 7 years, no moon effect <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li><strong>Old hand's rule</strong> (widely taught, opinion): \"Hunt the weather you have.\" Go every chance you get.</li><li><strong>Old hand's rule</strong> (opinion): \"Noon is for finding beds, not for napping.\"</li></ul><aside class=\"callout mistake\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Common mistakes</div><ul><li>Walking in at daylight. The deer were already up and leaving.</li><li>Planning around the moon.</li><li>Leaving at 10:00 on a cold rut day.</li></ul></aside><aside class=\"callout field\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Do this in the field</div><p>Each trip, log: time of each deer seen, temperature, wind, cloud, moon. After 10 trips, sort by hour.</p></aside></details>","<ul><li>Stewart and others 2002, <a href=\"https://academic.oup.com/jmammal/article/84/3/1076/905056\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">deer activity timing</a>, via research notes <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span></li></ul><ul><li>Germaine and others 2004, <a href=\"https://www.esf.edu/biology/faculty/documents/Germaineetal2004muledeerdaybedsites.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">mule deer day bed sites</a>, search preview, checked 2026-10-11 (60 to 80%)</li></ul><ul><li>Mule Deer Working Group fact sheet <a href=\"https://wildlife.utah.gov/pdf/deer/mdwg-17_winter_range_disturbance.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">17</a>, read directly, checked 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span></li></ul><ul><li>Webb and others 2010, International Journal of Ecology, <a href=\"https://doaj.org/article/98c06121b2744793be79f44614fcd27f\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">record</a>, search preview, checked 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span></li></ul><ul><li>Penn State Deer Research, <a href=\"https://deer.psu.edu/wandering-in-the-moonlight\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">wandering in the moonlight</a>, search preview, checked 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span></li></ul><ul><li>Steven Rinella, MeatEater (2018), <a href=\"https://themeateater.com/hunt/big-game/a-guide-to-hunting-mule-deer\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">A guide to hunting mule deer</a>, checked 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span></li></ul>","<ul><li>Bed site selection by desert mule deer, Southern Arizona 2001, <a href=\"https://experts.arizona.edu/en/publications/bed-site-selection-by-desert-mule-deer-in-southern-arizona/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">record</a>, search preview <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">60%</span></li></ul><ul><li>Stankowich 2008; Arizona 1988; Montana 1982; Idaho buck vulnerability: search previews, checked 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span></li></ul><ul><li>BC Hunting and Trapping Regulations Synopsis 2026 to 2028: page 11 (hours), via the <a href=\"#/s/rb-legal-methods\">Rule Book</a> <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span></li></ul><ul><li>Research notes: <code>research/2026-10-11-masterclass-mule-deer.md</code>.</li></ul>"]